---
import Term from "../Term.astro";
import Try from "../Try.astro";
import "../sternzeit/sternzeit.css";
import "./nachtgestirn.css";

/** The Moon through Earth's shadow: a row of discs across the next lunar eclipse, and the shadow's light by the radius. */
interface Props {
    id?: string;
}
const { id = "eclipse-row" } = Astro.props;
---

<figure class="tiles-figure" id={id} data-shadow>
    <div class="tiles-panel as-seen shadow-big">
        <canvas data-field="big" aria-label="The Moon in Earth's shadow at the slider's moment, rendered with WebGPU"></canvas>
        <svg data-field="outline" aria-hidden="true"></svg>
    </div>
    <label class="figure-slider" title="The moment through the eclipse, four hours either way from its greatest: drag, or turn the mouse wheel for a minute a notch">
        <span class="figure-slider-rail">
            <input type="range" data-field="offset" min="-240" max="240" step="1" value="0" aria-label="Minutes from the greatest eclipse" />
            <span class="figure-slider-scale" aria-hidden="true">{["−4", "0", "+4"].map((mark, i) => <span class="figure-slider-mark" style={`left: ${i * 50}%`}>{mark}{i !== 1 && <span class="figure-slider-unit"> h</span>}</span>)}</span>
        </span>
        <output data-field="offsetValue"></output>
    </label>
    <div class="tiles-panel as-seen">
        <canvas aria-label="The Moon at seven moments of a lunar eclipse, rendered with WebGPU"></canvas>
    </div>
    <ul class="tiles-labels" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(7, 1fr)">
        <li></li><li></li><li></li><li></li><li></li><li></li><li></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tiles-plot">
        <svg aria-hidden="true"></svg>
    </div>
    <p class="view-status"><button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-field="metered" aria-pressed="false" title="Expose each disc on its own, as the figure above meters, rather than all at one exposure">metered</button> <span data-field="note"></span></p>
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        Through Earth's shadow, the next lunar eclipse after the chosen moment, from Earth's center with north up:
        (a) the Moon at the slider's moment, metered, with the edges of the <Term of="Umbra">umbra</Term> and the
        penumbra drawn over it as it moves through them. (b) Seven moments from the Moon's first contact with the umbra
        to its last, all at one exposure: the umbra's when the eclipse is total, so the sunlit part burns out and the copper shows, the
        greatest moment's when it is partial. (c) What of the sunlight reaches
        the Moon, by the distance from the shadow's axis, red, green and blue, on a scale of stops: the{" "}
        <Term of="Penumbra">penumbra</Term>'s ramp, the umbra's copper and its turquoise rim, as nachtgestirn models
        them; the bar is the Moon's own width. The time is the page's clock.
        <Try label="New Year's Eve 2028, Berlin" set="date=2028-12-31T17:00Z&lat=52.52&lon=13.405&h=1" fig={id}>
            the total eclipse of that evening, the Moon's center marked in the shadow where it stands at the chosen
            moment, halfway in from the umbra's edge.
        </Try>
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
    import { shadowFigure } from "./shadow";

    for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("figure[data-shadow]")) shadowFigure(root);
</script>
